  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1110 AM CST Sat Nov 21 2026\n\nThe cold front will clear the area by mid Monday morning with \ncooler air moving in. Highs next week will be more on par with \nlate November with highs in the 50s instead of the 60s and 70s \nthat we've seen this week. Monday and Tuesday will be dry but a \ntrough will dig out of the plains towards the Gulf Coast. This \nwill bring medium (40- 60%) rain chances to our area on Wednesday.\nAs far as Thanksgiving day, some uncertainty remains with rain \nchances due to differences in the path of an upper low over the \nnorthern plains. The majority of the Euro members keep the upper \nlow farther north keeping our area dry. The majority of GEFS \nmembers bring the low further south bringing more rain chances for\nThanksgiving Day. All in all, the grand ensemble of GEFS, ENS, \nGEPS favor a drier solution for turkey day.",
